# Both merge outputs are gitignored, not just the master. The "master"
# (testimonials-merged.mp4, 172MB) fails GitHub's 100MB hard per-file limit
# outright; the "-web" compressed pass (~94MB) is technically under it but
# still an oversized, unreviewed binary nobody has asked to have in git
# history. Regenerate either with build_merge.sh — see README.
public/testimonials-merged.mp4
public/testimonials-merged-web.mp4

# The labelled review cut IS committed (~25MB) — it's the artifact the
# human compliance reviewer actually works from, and it's small enough.
!public/testimonials-review.mp4
